# Music Preference Modeling

*A machine learning project that models personal music taste from real listening behavior, using clustering, classification, and content-based recommendation.*

## Overview

This project analyzes my own Spotify listening history to understand my music taste and recommend new songs. Rather than relying on explicit ratings, it derives "taste scores" from real listening behavior (play count, completion rate, skip rate), then uses those scores to power a recommendation system and a classifier that predicts whether I'd love or dislike a song based on its audio characteristics.

The project touches unsupervised learning (clustering songs into mood groups), dimensionality reduction (visualizing those groups), supervised classification (predicting preference), and content-based recommendation (cosine similarity), using one real, personal dataset throughout.

## Data Sources

| Dataset | Original → Cleaned | Description |
|---|---:|---|
| Spotify Tracks Dataset (Kaggle, maharshipandya) | 114,000 → 79,921 | General catalog, Western/English-skewed |
| Spotify Multilingual Dataset (Kaggle, gauthamvijayaraj) | 62,317 → ~42,000 | English, Hindi, Tamil, Telugu, Malayalam, Korean |
| Spotify Indian Languages Dataset (Kaggle, gayathripullakhandam) | ~28,800 | 15 Indian languages, per-language CSVs |
| **Combined catalog** | **~150,674 songs** | Unified via a reusable cleaning/merging pipeline |
| My Spotify streaming history | 2021–2026, ~7,183 real plays after cleaning | Extended Streaming History export |

